## Plan

**Path:** `docs/plans/oracle/capped-whole-transcript-path.md`
**Slug:** `capped-whole-transcript-path` — no substring collision with `corpus-and-checkpoint`, `date-from-timestamp`, `run-scripts`, `whole-transcript-threshold`.
**Implements:** OD-5 → **R1001** (`covers: [R1001, R28]`), three slices, ~725 lines estimated.

It builds R28's saturated-video routing *together with* OD-5's cap: a video whose merged-and-capped excerpts reach 80% of its transcript is sent whole, unless its transcript would not fit in one bundle at `bundle_token_cap`, in which case it stays on the excerpt path. Routing goes in a new `submission.py`; `Excerpt` gains a defaulted `form` field so the bundle XML can say what each block is; the projection reports three path counts with their characters and tokens.

## What I had to guess at

All of it is in the plan's Uncertainties section, none of it ruled — a steward running unattended cannot stop or file a `BL-<n>`.

- **HIGH — scope.** OD-5 says `docs/plans/whole-transcript-threshold.md` "should be revised to carry R1000 and R1001". A steward may not write outside `docs/plans/oracle/`, and that plan's own text still reads *"do not build this slice until it is answered"* — nothing will lift that while nobody is awake. So this plan carries the whole behaviour and supersedes that slice. If the intended reading was a cap-only plan waiting on an owner revision, this plan is one slice too wide.
- **HIGH — `covers:` names R28** as well as R1001, duplicating the superseded plan's coverage, because this plan genuinely delivers R28's behaviour.
- **HIGH — the third count.** R1001 says "how many videos took each path"; I read the cap-forced fallback as its own path and put it in the `Projection` dataclass, since otherwise nothing observes OD-5 at all.
- **LOW** — routing in a new module rather than `excerpt.py`; the ratio measured on cue texts joined identically on both sides; "fits the cap" read as projected tokens, not characters; the 80% threshold left a module constant rather than a config lever; and build order after R1000's plan.

